    </div>
    <div id="p-0103" num="0102" class="description-paragraph">The use of lithium stearate additive in polypropylene can also improve membrane electrolyte wettability. Table 2 shows the average contact angle of the polypropylene membrane without additive and with 2% (20,000 ppm) and 5% (50,000 ppm) lithium stearate, using a propylene carbonate based electrolyte, which the most difficult electrolyte solvent for wetting. Reduction of contact angle from 91.5 to 81.4 degree is observed with 5% lithium stearate.</div>
